-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1116. `l4 batch` over an @export that reads `taken now`, a rule
-- of taken.l4 with no inputs that reads a ledger. Each row is a session of its
-- own (jl4/app/L4/Cli/Batch.hs, `processRow`: a fresh `runOneshot` for each),
-- so rows do not share an imported rule. A row is the file's directives that
-- `l4 batch` keeps, a #TRACE among them, and then its own #EVAL of the export,
-- and those do share it: the #TRACE here reads `taken now` after it commits
-- `taken`, and the row's answer, read against an empty ledger, is FALSE.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT taken

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Bob
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF peek, skip
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    go HAS mode IS A Mode
    buy

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`shop` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY buy PROVIDED NOT `taken now`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS TRUE HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`start` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY go m
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS (IF m EQUALS peek THEN NOT `taken now` ELSE TRUE) HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

@export default
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`closed now` MEANS `taken now`

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go skip AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2
